Dear Tom

Kingsholm Tonnage Ltd / Saltmarsh Shipping Ltd – MV Northern Star

Thank you for your letter of 23 September 2026. I have taken my client's instructions.

My client does not accept your calculation and rejects the offer of USD 96,300.00. Laytime ran from notice of readiness, which the master gave at 10:24 on Monday 3 August, and it expired at 10:24 on Sunday 9 August. Your client's attempt to start the clock the next morning does not change that.

Nor does the weather help your client. The Northern Star was already alongside the berth with her cargo accessible, and a swell does not stop a vessel in that position from discharging. The harbour's closure of its pilot station made no difference to her at all. My client therefore maintains its claim for USD 184,500.00, being 10.25 days at USD 18,000.00 a day.

My client will not agree to arbitration under clause 24 and is not obliged to. If this dispute is not settled, the courts of England will decide it.

Unless USD 184,500.00 is paid in cleared funds by 14 October 2026, my client will issue proceedings and will seek security for its claim, including if necessary by arresting the MV Curlew Bay, which we understand your client is selling. Please take this email as notice of that.

All of my client's rights are reserved.

Kind regards

